    <string name="bench_cpu_method">v1: deterministic 256-iteration arithmetic blocks with verified final states. One untimed warmup chunk. Three runs; warmup, JNI, safety checks and validation excluded from active duration. Iterations are algorithm steps, not CPU instructions or FLOPS.</string>
    <string name="bench_memory_method">v1: sequential copies between two reusable Rust buffers, 64 KiB each in conservative mode or 256 KiB each normally. Setup and full copy verification are outside active copy time. Reports actual bytes copied; caches and library copy routines affect results. Not physical RAM bandwidth.</string>
    <string name="interactive_title">Interactive Tests</string>
    <string name="interactive_privacy">Results are temporary and stay in memory. Manual observations and Android readings do not certify hardware health.</string>
